    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "People can now be retired from a date, and `bin/e2e` passes all 4 tests in the spec.\n\n**Stored data and server**\n- **Database:** a new migration `V16__person_retired.sql` adds a `retired_from` date to each person. It is empty for people who aren't retired.\n- **Retiring:** a new endpoint, `POST /api/sheets/{sheetId}/people/{personId}/retire`, sets the date. If no date is sent it uses the sheet's today. It writes `PERSON_RETIRED sheet=\u2026 by=\u2026 name=<name> from=<date>` to the audit file.\n- **Claims:** a claim dated after the retirement date is refused with a conflict error. This applies when adding a claim, when editing a claim's date, and to quick add, since quick add goes through the same code. Claims dated on or before the retirement date are still accepted, even if added later.\n\n**Screen**\n- **Toggle:** there is a \"Show retired\" checkbox above the people list. It starts off when the screen opens. Its setting is kept in the people service, not the list component, so loading a sheet doesn't reset it.\n- **Hidden rows:** with the toggle off, retired people have no row at all. Their claims still count in the per-person and sheet totals.\n- **New columns:** each row shows Retired (yes/no) and Retired from.\n- **Retire control:** each row has a date input and a Retire button. If the date is left empty, the sheet's today is used. A refused retire shows the row's existing error message, which is cleared by the next action on that row.\n\nA few choices the request didn't settle:\n- Retiring someone who is already retired just changes the date and writes another audit line.\n- Retiring doesn't check for claims the person already has dated after the new date.\n- Opening, settling and voiding existing claims are not blocked by retirement.\n- Retiring writes no ROLLUP line, because it doesn't change any figures; the test's expected audit lines agree.\n- When a claim is refused for being after retirement, the screen shows the general \"Could not add that claim.\" message, not one that names the retirement.",
